; RESULT (3 runs, Apple M4 Max, verdict 511 all three, worst form-vs-gpu delta 0.000006 all three —
; every one of 424 repetitions checked against every one of 3072 real output positions of the ONE
; computed-once reference, no sampling): gpu_busy_us_total = 2184810 / 2181703 / 2187635us
; (avg 2184716us), versus the rows=8 baseline's verified 890987us — a 2.452x increase in GPU-device
; time for 384x more real compute (rows 8->3072). That is DRAMATICALLY sub-linear: PARTIALLY
; CONFIRMS the fixed-barrier-cost hypothesis in the narrow sense the header below poses it (cost did
; NOT scale with compute, so much of the rows=8 floor was not real work) — but the hypothesis's
; INTENDED PAYLOAD, that this mechanism explains DS4's absolute advantage, is REFUTED BY MAGNITUDE:
; per-dispatch (848 total, the same basis the ~40-50x history figure uses), cost went 1050.7us
; (rows=8) -> 2576.8us (rows=3072) — the gap to DS4's ~20-26us/barrier grew from ~40-53x to
; ~99-129x, roughly DOUBLING, not closing. Per-repetition/per-barrier (424, DS4's own counting
; unit), 2101.4us -> 5153.6us, gap ~81-105x -> ~198-258x. Doing 384x more real work per barrier made
; the probe's cost-per-FLOP ~157x better (384/2.452) while making its ABSOLUTE per-barrier cost
; ~2.45x WORSE and the gap to DS4's absolute floor ~2.45x WIDER. If "more real work dilutes the same
; fixed tax" were DS4's whole advantage, matching or exceeding DS4's typical per-barrier compute
; density (this probe's single 3072x3072 matvec is not smaller than what sits between many of DS4's
; own barriers) should have moved this probe's absolute number toward DS4's floor — it moved away.
; The elimination chain's four tested hypotheses (residency, stage-A parallelism, host-timing
; artifact, fixed-barrier-cost-diluted-by-compute) are now each precisely accounted for: three
; refuted outright, and the fourth confirmed only in its narrow scaling-shape sense while its
; explanatory claim is refuted by absolute magnitude. The real mechanism behind DS4's ~20-26us/barrier
; floor remains open and is NOT any of the five structural differences this chain has tested —
; candidates it did not yet test: cross-layer dispatch overlap/pipeline depth (DS4 interleaves many
; independent layers' work across 1510-1844 barriers, giving the GPU far more concurrent work to hide
; latency behind than this probe's single strictly-serial 2-stage chain), persistent-encoder or
; pipeline-state-object residency effects, or GPU clock/power-state differences between a short
; isolated probe and a long sustained real decode. Named precisely, not chased further here.
;
; form-native-decode-chain-fullrow.fk — the fixed-barrier-cost-vs-real-compute test against
; form-native-decode-chain.fk (PR #431, unpooled baseline) and form-native-decode-chain-pooled.fk
; (PR #432, REFUTED) / form-native-decode-chain-tg.fk (PR #433, REFUTED). Those two ruled out buffer
; residency and stage-A kernel parallelism as the source of the ~1049us/dispatch GPU-device-busy
; floor (PR #434 proved that floor is genuinely GPU-device-resident, not a host-timing artifact, by
; adding `gpu_busy_us_total` to metal_status from `[cb GPUEndTime]-[cb GPUStartTime]` — the same
; properties DS4's own harvest() reads). This file tests the one remaining structural difference
; named in that chain: DS4's real barriers (metal_dsv4_stack.sh, ~20-26us/barrier average) sit
; between MUCH LARGER real computations than this probe's stage B, which the unpooled file's own
; header scoped to 8 of the real 3072 attn_q.weight rows — for HOST-SIDE Form-reference
; verification cost on a tree-walking runtime, not GPU dispatch cost (that file's SCOPE section is
; explicit about this and is the reason a wider run was always the next honest step, not a redesign).
;
; THE HYPOTHESIS UNDER TEST: if memoryBarrierWithScope:.buffers's real hardware cost is roughly
; FIXED per call (a genuine pipeline drain, largely independent of how much real compute preceded
; it), then the unpooled file's ~1049us/dispatch average (890987us / 848 dispatches, PR #434's
; verified gpu_busy_us_total) is mostly FIXED BARRIER OVERHEAD at rows=8's tiny stage-B compute —
; and DS4's ~20-26us/barrier isn't a cheaper barrier mechanism, it is the SAME fixed cost divided by
; far more real compute per call. Scaling stage B from 8 to the full 3072 real rows (384x the real
; compute, SAME barrier pattern, SAME n=424 repetitions) tests this directly: if gpu_busy_us_total
; grows roughly PROPORTIONALLY with the added compute, the ~1049us floor was mostly real work (the
; hypothesis is REFUTED). If it grows only a little relative to 384x, the floor was mostly fixed
; barrier overhead now being diluted (the hypothesis is CONFIRMED, and DS4's real advantage has a
; concrete mechanism: more real work per barrier, not a cheaper barrier).
;
; THE TWO REAL STAGES: identical to form-native-decode-chain.fk in every respect (same kernels
; called, not retyped; same real llama3.2:3b bytes; same barrier_before=0 on stage A / 1 on stage B;
; same n=424; same single metal_batch_concurrent/metal_sync framing). The ONLY change is
; `fndcf-rows` = 3072 instead of 8 — the full real Q projection width, not a placeholder. q4k-msl.fk's
; q4m-matvec-body kernel was read to confirm this is legitimate: its dispatch guard is
; `if (i >= rows) return;`, parameterized entirely by the `rows` uniform bound at enqueue time
; (md-bind16) and by the `metal_enqueue pipeB ... rows` thread count passed from this file — nothing
; about row width is hardcoded in the kernel or the binding shape. fk-metal-carrier.m's dispatch path
; (fk_metal_enqueue_external, ~line 707-735) uses `dispatchThreads:MTLSizeMake(threads,1,1)
; threadsPerThreadgroup:MTLSizeMake(min(maxTotalThreadsPerThreadgroup,threads),1,1)` — Apple GPUs
; (M-series, family 4+) support non-uniform threadgroups under dispatchThreads, so 3072 threads is
; not a new code path, just a wider grid.
;
; THE CORRECTNESS TRADEOFF, CALIBRATED, NOT GUESSED. The unpooled file scoped to 8 rows specifically
; because verifying every repetition's output against Form's own independent Q4_K dequant+dot
; (q4m-flat-at) costs real wall time on this tree-walking runtime, and the header named that as the
; open question a wider run would have to answer. Rather than assume the cost is prohibitive at
; full width, it was measured directly: a throwaway timing probe computed the SAME reference loop
; this file uses (fndcf-ref-rows) at rows=8, 64, and 256 against the SAME real tensor window,
; isolated from GPU dispatch entirely. Results: rows=8 -> 173ms, rows=64 -> 1386ms (8.01x rows,
; 8.01x time), rows=256 -> 5561ms (32x rows, 32.1x time) — clean LINEAR scaling, ~21.7ms per row
; (173/8=21.6, 1386/64=21.66, 5561/256=21.72). At rows=3072 that extrapolates to ~66.7s for the ONE
; reference computation this file still does only ONCE (inputs are identical across all 424
; repetitions, exactly as the unpooled file's own header establishes — a genuine race would show up
; as a repetition whose stage-B output differs from the others, which checking every repetition
; against one Form-computed reference is built to catch, without paying N times for the dequant
; itself). That one-time ~67s cost — and the per-repetition readback+diff cost below it, which is
; pure elementwise subtract/abs/max over already-dequantized floats, not a second dequant pass, and
; extrapolates from the unpooled file's own 22ms/424reps-at-8-wide to roughly 8.5s at
; 424reps-at-3072-wide — both land ENTIRELY in Part D/E, AFTER the single metal_sync (ts1) and
; BEFORE this file's own verify timer starts, i.e. entirely OUTSIDE the GPU-timed window this
; experiment measures (alloc-ms, enqueue-ms, sync-ms, and metal_status's gpu_busy_us_total). Given
; that headroom, this file does NOT sample: it checks EVERY ONE of the 424 repetitions against
; EVERY ONE of the 3072 real output positions of the ONE computed-once reference — the exact same
; completeness the unpooled file already provides at rows=8, just wider, because the calibration
; showed the honest full check is affordable rather than requiring an under-verified shortcut.
;
; THE BARRIER: unchanged from the unpooled file — MTLBarrierScopeBuffers is coarse (settles ALL
; buffer memory effects encoded before the barrier point, not only the matching pair), named there
; and not repeated in full here; see form-native-decode-chain.fk lines ~26-40 for the complete
; argument. This file makes no new claim about the barrier's semantics, only about what sits either
; side of it.
;
; NOT A BAND, same reasoning as its kin: a wall-clock/GPU-device-time duration is not
; four-way-provable, and Metal has no Go/Rust/TS arm to check a microsecond against. The reference
; Q4_K dequant path (eqr-at / str_byte_at) is the same TWO-ARM byte door (fkwu + Go) named in the
; unpooled file's own header — no new correctness claim beyond what q4k-msl-band.fk already proves
; for the transcription is added here; this file adds no new pure-Form arithmetic shape (no new
; band needed, per form-native-decode-chain-pooled.fk's identical precedent for `mod`-based reuse
; not needing a fresh proof).
;
; RUN:
;   cd form && ./validate.sh form-stdlib/tests/moe-gate-band.fk   # (or any band) builds ./fkwu
;   cd .. && ./fkwu form/form-stdlib/form-native-decode-chain-fullrow.fk
;
; Kin: form-stdlib/form-native-decode-chain.fk (the rows=8 baseline this file widens, byte-identical
;      stages/barrier-pattern/n; PR #431's own SCOPE section is what this file's calibration
;      answers), form-stdlib/form-native-decode-chain-pooled.fk / -tg.fk (PR #432/#433, both
;      REFUTED — buffer residency and stage-A parallelism), native/metal/fk-metal-carrier.m
;      (metal_status's gpu_busy_us_total, PR #434 — the real device-time number this file reads,
;      same as the unpooled file; fk_metal_enqueue_external's dispatchThreads sizing, read here to
;      confirm rows=3072 needs no code change), form-stdlib/q4k-msl.fk (q4m-matvec-body — stage B's
;      kernel, read here to confirm `rows` fully parameterizes dispatch width; q4m-flat-at — the
;      reference this file's correctness check reads through, at full width, calibrated above),
;      native/metal/metal_dsv4_stack.sh (~line 764-800 — DS4's own per-barrier average this file's
;      result is measured against).
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/format-arith.fk form-stdlib/metal-door.fk form-stdlib/equireach.fk form-stdlib/equireach-gguf.fk form-stdlib/gguf-meta.fk native/metal/whole-tensor-residency.fk form-stdlib/llama-decode-msl.fk form-stdlib/llama-numerics.fk form-stdlib/form-native-decode.fk form-stdlib/q4k-msl.fk

(do
    ; SAME N as the unpooled file — same real per-forward dispatch count, so the two measurements
    ; sit next to each other on the same N.
    (defn fndcf-n () 424)

    ; stage B's real output width — the FULL real Q projection, not the unpooled file's 8-row scope.
    ; This is the ONLY structural change from form-native-decode-chain.fk.
    (defn fndcf-rows () 3072)

    ; ================= locating the real Q4_K tensor, verified against the LIVE file =================
    (defn fndcf-q-abs (src) (egg-tensor-abs src (wtr-alignment) "blk.0.attn_q.weight"))
    (defn fndcf-q-type (src) (egg-ti-type src (egg-find-tensor src "blk.0.attn_q.weight")))
    (defn fndcf-q-dim0 (src) (egg-ti-dim src (egg-find-tensor src "blk.0.attn_q.weight") 0))
    ; SAME formula as the unpooled file's fndc-q-row-bytes (a Q4_K row is (cols/256) superblocks of
    ; 144 bytes) — duplicated rather than called cross-file, same precedent as -pooled.fk /-tg.fk
    ; (form-native-decode-chain.fk is a live self-executing witness, not preluded by its kin).
    (defn fndcf-q-row-bytes (cols) (mul (div cols 256) 144))

    ; ================= the reference: Form's OWN independent Q4_K matvec, computed ONCE =================
    ; Identical shape to the unpooled file's fndc-ref-*, calibrated above to ~67s at rows=3072 —
    ; affordable because it runs exactly ONCE regardless of n=424 (inputs are identical every rep).
    (defn fndcf-ref-dot-loop (qsrc row cols j n xs acc)
        (if (eq j n) acc
            (fndcf-ref-dot-loop qsrc row cols (add j 1) n (tail xs)
                (add acc (mul (q4m-flat-at qsrc 0 (add (mul row cols) j)) (head xs))))))
    (defn fndcf-ref-dot (qsrc row cols xs) (fndcf-ref-dot-loop qsrc row cols 0 cols xs 0.0))

    (defn fndcf-ref-rows-loop (qsrc row rows cols xs acc)
        (if (eq row rows) (reverse acc)
            (fndcf-ref-rows-loop qsrc (add row 1) rows cols xs
                (cons (fndcf-ref-dot qsrc row cols xs) acc))))
    (defn fndcf-ref-rows (qsrc rows cols xs) (fndcf-ref-rows-loop qsrc 0 rows cols xs (list)))

    ; ================= N fresh buffer pairs: stage-A output (d wide) + stage-B output (rows wide) ====
    (defn fndcf-alloc-loop (i n d rows acc-hy acc-hz)
        (if (ge i n) (list (reverse acc-hy) (reverse acc-hz))
            (fndcf-alloc-loop (add i 1) n d rows
                (cons (metal_buf_alloc (mul d 4)) acc-hy)
                (cons (metal_buf_alloc (mul rows 4)) acc-hz))))

    ; ================= the timed enqueue loop: stage A (barrier=0) then stage B (barrier=1) =========
    (defn fndcf-enq-loop (i n pipeA pipeB hx hg hqb d ebits rows cols hys hzs acc)
        (if (ge i n) acc
            (fndcf-enq-loop (add i 1) n pipeA pipeB hx hg hqb d ebits rows cols (tail hys) (tail hzs)
                (add acc
                    (add (metal_enqueue pipeA (md-bind (list hx hg (head hys)) (list d ebits)) 1)
                         (metal_enqueue pipeB
                             (md-bind16 (list hqb (head hys) (head hzs)) (list rows cols) 0 0 0 1)
                             rows))))))

    ; ================= readback + per-repetition verification against the ONE Form reference =======
    ; FULL width, EVERY repetition — no sampling. See header calibration for why this is affordable.
    (defn fndcf-verify-loop (hzs rows ref-y worst)
        (if (eq (len hzs) 0) worst
            (do
                (let bytes (metal_buf_read (head hzs) 0 (mul rows 4)))
                (let gy (ewl-gain bytes 0 rows))
                (let d (fnd-maxdiff ref-y gy))
                (fndcf-verify-loop (tail hzs) rows ref-y (if (gt d worst) d worst)))))

    (defn fndcf-run ()
        (do
            (let live (md-door-live?))
            (let path (fnd-blob-path))
            (let src (fnd-src path))
            (let d (fnd-dmodel src))
            (let eps (fnd-eps src))
            (let ebits (md-f32-bits eps))
            (let gnabs (fnd-norm-abs src path))
            (let n (fndcf-n))
            (let rows (fndcf-rows))
            (let cols d)

            ; verified against the LIVE file (not trusted): Q4_K, 2 dims, dim0 = cols.
            (let qtype (fndcf-q-type src))
            (let qdim0 (fndcf-q-dim0 src))
            (let qabs (fndcf-q-abs src))

            ; ---- resident, built ONCE: real gain, synthetic input, real Q4_K weight window ---------
            (let hg (metal_buf_from_file path gnabs (mul d 4)))
            (let hx (metal_buf_alloc (mul d 4)))
            (let wx (metal_buf_write hx 0 (fnd-x-bytes d)))
            (let hqb (metal_buf_from_file path qabs (mul rows (fndcf-q-row-bytes cols))))
            (let pipeA (metal_pipeline (fnd-msl) "form_rmsnorm_f32"))
            (let pipeB (metal_pipeline
                (str_concat "#include <metal_stdlib>\n" (q4m-matvec-msl "form_matvec_q4k_stageb"))
                "form_matvec_q4k_stageb"))

            ; ---- A: N buffer-pair allocations, timed alone -----------------------------------------
            (let ta0 (now_unix_ms))
            (let bufs (fndcf-alloc-loop 0 n d rows (list) (list)))
            (let hys (nth bufs 0))
            (let hzs (nth bufs 1))
            (let ta1 (now_unix_ms))

            ; ---- ARM: outside both timed windows, exactly as the unpooled probe does ------------
            (let armed (metal_batch_concurrent))

            ; ---- B: N*2 real dispatches enqueued, A(barrier=0) then B(barrier=1) per repetition ----
            (let te0 (now_unix_ms))
            (let ok-count (fndcf-enq-loop 0 n pipeA pipeB hx hg hqb d ebits rows cols hys hzs 0))
            (let te1 (now_unix_ms))

            ; ---- C: ONE sync for the whole batch -----------------------------------------------------
            (let ts0 (now_unix_ms))
            (let drained (metal_sync))
            (let ts1 (now_unix_ms))

            ; ---- D: the Form reference, computed ONCE (inputs are identical across all N reps) ------
            ; calibrated at ~67s for rows=3072 — outside every timed window above and below.
            (let gains (ewl-gain (eqr-of-file path gnabs (mul d 4)) 0 d))
            (let form-y0 (ln-rmsnorm (fnd-x-list d) gains eps))
            (let qsrc (eqr-of-file path qabs (mul rows (fndcf-q-row-bytes cols))))
            (let ref-y (fndcf-ref-rows qsrc rows cols form-y0))

            ; ---- E: read back and verify EVERY repetition's stage-B output against the ONE reference
            (let tr0 (now_unix_ms))
            (let worst (fndcf-verify-loop hzs rows ref-y 0.0))
            (let tr1 (now_unix_ms))

            (list live n rows cols qtype qdim0 armed ok-count drained
                  (sub ta1 ta0) (sub te1 te0) (sub ts1 ts0) (sub tr1 tr0) worst)))

    (defn fndcf-us-per (ms n) (floor (div (mul ms 1000) n)))

    (defn fndcf-show ()
        (do
            (let r (fndcf-run))
            (let live (nth r 0))
            (let n (nth r 1))
            (let rows (nth r 2))
            (let cols (nth r 3))
            (let qtype (nth r 4))
            (let qdim0 (nth r 5))
            (let armed (nth r 6))
            (let ok-count (nth r 7))
            (let drained (nth r 8))
            (let alloc-ms (nth r 9))
            (let enq-ms (nth r 10))
            (let sync-ms (nth r 11))
            (let verify-ms (nth r 12))
            (let worst (nth r 13))
            (let ndisp (mul n 2))
            (let batch-ms (add (add alloc-ms enq-ms) sync-ms))

            (print_str (metal_status))
            (print_str (str_concat "door-live " (if live "true" "false")))
            (print_str (str_concat "attn_q.weight type(want=12 Q4_K) " (int_to_str qtype)))
            (print_str (str_concat "attn_q.weight dim0(want=3072) " (int_to_str qdim0)))
            (print_str (str_concat "batch_concurrent armed(want=1) " (int_to_str armed)))
            (print_str (str_concat "n repetitions " (int_to_str n)))
            (print_str (str_concat "rows(stage B real output width, FULL) " (int_to_str rows)))
            (print_str (str_concat "cols(d_model) " (int_to_str cols)))
            (print_str (str_concat "total dispatches(2*n) " (int_to_str ndisp)))
            (print_str (str_concat "ok-count(want=2n) " (int_to_str ok-count)))
            (print_str (str_concat "drained(want=2n) " (int_to_str drained)))
            (print_str (str_concat "worst max-abs-delta form-vs-gpu(all n reps, all 3072 positions) " (float_to_str worst)))
            (print_str (str_concat "alloc-ms " (int_to_str alloc-ms)))
            (print_str (str_concat "enqueue-ms " (int_to_str enq-ms)))
            (print_str (str_concat "sync-ms " (int_to_str sync-ms)))
            (print_str (str_concat "verify(readback+diff)-ms(" (str_concat (int_to_str n) " reps, full width) ")))
            (print_str (int_to_str verify-ms))
            (print_str (str_concat "alloc+enqueue+sync-ms " (int_to_str batch-ms)))
            (print_str (str_concat "us/dispatch enqueue-only " (int_to_str (fndcf-us-per enq-ms ndisp))))
            (print_str (str_concat "us/dispatch enqueue+sync " (int_to_str (fndcf-us-per (add enq-ms sync-ms) ndisp))))
            (print_str (str_concat "us/repetition enqueue-only " (int_to_str (fndcf-us-per enq-ms n))))
            (print_str (str_concat "us/repetition enqueue+sync " (int_to_str (fndcf-us-per (add enq-ms sync-ms) n))))

            (if live (if (eq armed 1) (if (eq ok-count ndisp) (if (eq drained ndisp) (if (lt worst 0.01) 1 0) 0) 0) 0) 0)))

    (fndcf-show))
